  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so the priority is to establish a performance baseline against which all subsequent configurations can be meaningfully compared. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest possible configuration: it uses the most basic encoder (PCA), requires no aggregation or fusion, and tests only the raw RNA signal. This serves as the 'null model' for the study. Its result will clarify: (1) the performance floor of the task, (2) whether RNA alone carries sufficient signal, and (3) the magnitude of headroom available for more complex encoders, multiprofile aggregation, or multimodal fusion. Establishing this anchor first is the most efficient use of the first experiment under a limited budget, because every later comparison (better RNA encoder, adding image, adding aggregation, adding fusion) becomes interpretable only relative to a known single-modality, single-profile baseline."
}

